# Pairs with AckedWritesServed. A write lands on the old copy after its
# cluster cut over (a write path that kept the pre-cutover routing), so the
# acknowledged write is lost from the copy the tree now serves.
MODULE: AckedWritesServedWriteToRetiredCopy
TARGET: AckedWritesServed
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a post-cutover write is applied to the retired copy
PERTURBS: Write

--- FIND
       IN /\ data' = [data EXCEPT ![c][p] = @ \cup {w}]
          /\ log' = [log EXCEPT ![c][p] = @ \cup {w}]
--- REPLACE
       IN \* MUTATION: the data lands on the old copy whatever the alias says.
          /\ data' = [data EXCEPT ![c]["old"] = @ \cup {w}]
          /\ log' = [log EXCEPT ![c]["old"] = @ \cup {w}]
--- END
